v0.17.0 release — the REPL gets out of your way: it runs on the terminal's normal screen so the mouse wheel scrolls the transcript and ↑/↓ alone recall history (--altscreen opts back in), the /config wizard no longer leaks its keystrokes into the prompt (no ghost re-run, no dead input afterwards) and cleans its output up when it finishes, assistant markdown is rendered (**bold**, `code`, # headings, fences) as it streams, and tool calls live on the status band instead of the transcript
